This transfers convergence of moment generating functions to #ponder("probability.convergence-in-distribution")[convergence in distribution]. To prove $X_n stretch(->)^((d)) Z$ it therefore suffices to establish $EE[ee^(theta X_n)] -> EE[ee^(theta Z)]$ for every $theta in RR$, together with finiteness of the limiting transform for some $theta != 0$; this is how the #ponder("probability.central-limit-theorem")[central limit theorem] is proved.
